      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To solve this problem, we first need to determine how long it takes the train to completely exit the tunnel and then use that information to find the length of the tunnel.\n\nThe total travel time of the train, including both the arrival and departure hours, is 3 minutes. Since there are 60 minutes in an hour, we can convert the travel time to hours:\n\n3 minutes = (3 / 60) hours\n= 0.05 hours\n\nNow, we know that the train travels at a speed of 60 miles per hour and needs 0.05 hours to completely exit the tunnel. To find the length of the tunnel, we can calculate the distance covered by the train in that time:\n\nDistance = Speed * Time\n= 60 miles per hour * 0.05 hours\n= 3 miles\n\nThis distance represents the length of the tunnel (excluding the front portion of the train). Since the tail of the train exits the tunnel 3 miles from the front, and considering the total length of the train, we have:\n\nLength of Tunnel = Length of Train + Length of Tail\n= 1 mile + 3 miles\n= 4 miles\n\nTherefore, the tunnel is 4 miles in length.",
