      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "1 mile. Since we are told that \"the tail of a 1-mile long train\" exits the tunnel \"exactly 3 minutes after the front of the train entered the tunnel,\" we know that this is a linear recurrence:\n\nLength of tunnel + Speed of train = Distance traveled + Detail length of train exited\n\nWe are told that the speed of the train is 60 miles per hour and that the length of the train is 1 mile. If we let D = Distance traveled and Detail = Detail length of the train exited, we have:\n\nD = 60 miles per hour\n        = 1 miles\nD + 1 = 3 miles\nD + Detail = 3 miles\nD = 2 miles\n\nTherefore, the length of the tunnel is \\boxed{2} miles.",
