    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "We start by finding the number of miles through which the front of the train has traveled in 3 minutes. Since there are 60 minutes in an hour, or 120 seconds in a minute, the train has traveled $\\frac{120}{3}=40$ minutes, or $\\boxed{2}$ miles.\nTo solve this problem, we begin by calculating the distance traveled by the front of the train in 3 minutes. Since the speed of the train is 60 miles per hour, or $\\frac{60}{60}=1$ mile per minute, the front of the train has traveled $40 \\times 1 = 40$ miles in 3 minutes. The length of the train is added on before the front exits the tunnel, so the length of the tunnel is $40 - 1 = \\boxed{39}$ miles.",
