    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "First, let's convert the train's speed from miles per hour to miles per minute. We know that there are 60 minutes in an hour, so we divide 60 miles per hour by 60 to get 1 mile per minute.\n\nNext, let's determine how far the train travels in 3 minutes. Since the train travels 1 mile every minute, in 3 minutes it will have traveled 3 miles.\n\nNow, let's consider the entire journey from the time the front of the train enters the tunnel until the rear exits. The train's total length (1 mile) plus the length of the tunnel equals the distance the train has traveled in 3 minutes. So, if the train had traveled 1 mile in 3 minutes without being stopped in the tunnel, then the combined length of the train and the tunnel must also be 1 mile, but since the question states the tunnel exits at 3 minutes after the front enters, the answer must be the sum of 1 mile (train's length) and 2 miles (tunnel length). Therefore, the tunnel must be 2 miles long.\n\n$\\boxed{2}$",
